2025-12-20  David

	* Version 1.2.0 released

	* csv: Added 'pick' subcommand for selecting specific rows by number
	- Syntax: csv pick [-a] [-f file] row1 row2 ...
	- Rows are 1-indexed (row 1 = first data row)
	- Use -a to include header and comments in output
	- Supports stdin when -f not specified

	* csv: Changed wc output format to "Rows: N  Columns: N  Bytes: N"

	* csv: The -a flag now includes comment lines in wc row count

	* csv: Added --version (-V) option

	* csv.1: Updated man page with pick command and wc output format

	* README, NEWS: Updated documentation

2025-11-29  David

	* Version 1.1.0 released

	* csv: Added +N options for head and tail commands
	- csv tail +N: Start from row N (1-indexed) and print to end
	- csv head +N: Show all but last N data rows
	- Follows POSIX tail convention

	* csv.1: Updated man page with +N option documentation

	* README: Updated with +N usage examples

2025-11-26  David

	* Version 1.0.0 released

	* Initial implementation with head, tail, wc, cut commands

	* Row-aware CSV parsing using Python csv module

	* Support for comment lines starting with #

	* stdin/stdout support for pipeline usage

	* GNU-compliant packaging with Makefile
